  "id": "Compound::DB00997 - Disease::DOID:4045",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the development of Muscle Cancer through a chain of interactions involving Methotrexate, which acts as a mediator in the pathway. The evidence suggests that Doxorubicin causes Pneumocystis Jirovecii Pneumonia, which is in turn caused by Methotrexate, and Methotrexate is known to treat Muscle Cancer. This indicates a potential indirect relationship where Doxorubicin may influence the progression of Muscle Cancer via Methotrexate. The shared lowest common ancestors—Hydroxides and Enzyme Inhibitors—suggest a common mechanism or pathway that connects Doxorubicin to Methotrexate and ultimately to Muscle Cancer. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Methotrexate as a bridge between Doxorubicin and Muscle Cancer, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
